THIS IS NOT AN END-USER LICENCE. It says what may be done with this source, and says nothing
about what somebody who downloads a Spark build may do with it. That is a different document
and it has not been written yet; it needs a lawyer rather than a placeholder.

Versions of Spark published before 2026-09-09 were released under the MIT licence. That grant
is irrevocable for anyone who took a copy, and nothing here reaches backwards to withdraw it.

Spark is built on third-party components, several of which carry obligations that are entirely
unaffected by the above. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists all of them. In particular Spark links
OpenCascade under the LGPL-2.1 with the Open CASCADE exception, which obliges a standing offer
of that library's source and the ability to relink against your own build of it; both are
honoured at https://github.com/harilalmn/Spark-Releases.
